\subsection{Environment and Training Details}
\label{sec:env_details}

All experiments use Walker Walk and Cheetah Run from the DeepMind Control Suite (DMC; \citealt{tassa2018dmcontrol}) with proprioceptive observations. Walker Walk (6-joint biped) serves as the primary environment with the full factorial design; Cheetah Run (6-joint runner) serves as a severity probe (CIVO at $8$--$70\times$ NVE vs.\ $2$--$5\times$ on Walker). The baseline runs for 500K steps; treatments run for 105K steps. All hyperparameters follow DreamerV3 defaults \citep{hafner2023dreamerv3} ($d{=}32$ temporal embedding; Appendix~\ref{sec:hyperparameters}). Training uses a single NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 GPU (${\sim}80$ GPU-hours). The codebase extends the official DreamerV3 implementation\footnote{\url{https://github.com/danijar/dreamerv3}, accessed March 2026.} with the variable-rate modules described in \S\ref{sec:variable_rate}.

